---
description: ContextTrim project rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- Stack: Node 20+, TypeScript, run with tsx. No framework, no database, no network calls.
- Allowed dependencies: js-tiktoken, ignore, typescript, tsx, @types/node. Ask before adding anything else.
- Use node:util parseArgs for the CLI. Plain ANSI codes for color.
- Core modules (walker, tokens, analyze, waste, rules) are pure: they take input and return data. Only cli.ts and fix.ts print or write.
- Never modify or delete user files. Writing is limited to .cursorignore, .cursor/rules/project.mdc (only with --write), and contexttrim-report.html.
- `fix` and `rules` are dry-run by default. Writing requires --write plus a y/N confirm unless --yes.
- Every number shown that is an estimate says "estimated". Print skipped files and caps; never hide them.
- Read thresholds and patterns from waste-rules.json and models.json, not hardcoded.
- Handle errors with short readable messages, no stack traces.
- Keep files small and simple. No premature abstractions.
- Work in the phases defined in PRD.md. Stop after each phase so I can test. Commit after each working phase.
